  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Psycho-social support for IDPs/refugees in Ukraine and eastern Slovakia (Phase 3)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the project is to improve psycho-social state of refugees/IDPs and people directly affected by the war in Ukraine. The outcome of the intervention is to achieve a tangible impact on the target group in helping vulnerable refugees/IDP to better cope with war traumas, strengthening their resilience and better integrating into host communities. This will be achieved by providing tailor-made psycho-social support services via employed and trained psycho-social workers and psychologists. 

The project is a &#x201c;Phase 3&#x201d; continuation of an existing psycho-social intervention starting as an emergency response in May 2022, a few months after the outbreak of the full-scale war in Ukraine. The project is being delivered in five locations by 5 local implementing partners from the Caritas network with a strong focus on Ukraine. 

The Phase 3 project will ensure the continuation of much-needed psycho-social services and build on the experiences build-up in the previous project phases. The activities will rely primarily on the existing trained psycho-social staff. In Phase 3, the project will undergo a geographic re-focus and will be enriched by important elements ensuring a qualitative re-shape. T</narrative>
  </description>
